# Custom domains of projects (ADR-024) on an Edge host, imported at the top
# level of the host Caddyfile, beside the wildcard sites. sakala-edge writes one
# site per verified domain into custom-domains.caddy, each starting with
# `import sakala_custom_domain_tls`, so this snippet must be defined first and
# keep that name. Create an empty custom-domains.caddy at install so Caddy
# starts before the first sync. See docs/EDGE.md.
#
# Certificates for these names come from Let's Encrypt through HTTP-01 or
# TLS-ALPN-01 on this host: port 80 and 443 must be reachable, and the host
# Caddyfile must not set the global acme_dns option, which Caddy would copy
# into this issuer. ACME_EMAIL comes from Caddy's environment; sakala-edge
# validates with a placeholder value.
(sakala_custom_domain_tls) {
	tls {
		issuer acme {
			dir https://acme-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory
			email {$ACME_EMAIL}
		}
	}
}

import /var/lib/sakala-edge/custom-domains.caddy
